<title>SOUTH AFRICA: S.African mohair prices mixed at last summer sale.</title>
<headline>S.African mohair prices mixed at last summer sale.</headline>
<dateline>PORT ELIZABETH, South Africa 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>South African mohair prices for the last summer sale were mixed, the Mohair Board said on Wednesday. There was still very good demand for sale.</p>
<p>Of the 1,588 bales offered 58 percent was sold.</p>
<p>Approximate prices in South African cents a kg:</p>
<p>Adults	  long	 1,840-2,500	(2,100-3,650)</p>
<p>		  medium     1,700-1,852	(1,800-2,000)</p>
<p>		  short	1,700-1,820	(1,750-1,890)</p>
<p>Young Goats   long	 2,400-4,010	(2,300-2,800)</p>
<p>		  medium     1,760-2,740	(2,050-2,050)</p>
<p>		  short	     -	     (     -     )</p>
<p>Fine Kids     long	 8,000-14,500     (7,600-12,850)</p>
<p>		  medium     4,460-8,050	(4,252-6,000)</p>
<p>		  short	3,000-4,752	(3,800-4,600)</p>
<p>The first winter sale of the season is scheduled for August 19, 1997.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom, +27-11 482 1003</p>
</text>
